      <h1 class="article-title">The Martyrdom of Ignatius</h1>
      <p class="article-dek faith-doc-dek">Anonymous &middot; c. 2nd–4th century</p>
      
      <p class="faith-doc-description">An account of the arrest, journey, and execution of Ignatius of Antioch in the Colosseum at Rome under Emperor Trajan. Its historical reliability is debated, but it preserves the early church’s memory of one of its most celebrated martyrs.</p>
