          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The Martyrdom of Ignatius narrates the arrest, journey, and execution of the bishop of Antioch in the Roman Colosseum under Emperor Trajan. Its date and historical reliability are debated, but it preserves the early church’s memory of one of its most celebrated witnesses. Whether composed shortly after the events or embellished in later centuries, the text stands as testimony to the early Christian conviction that the blood of the martyrs is the seed of the church.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
